<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Later Hojo clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1495 CE – 1590 CE (approx.) · capital Odawara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Kanto domain of the Later Hojo, five generations of lords ruling from Odawara whose efficient administration made them the strongest power in eastern Japan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-soun">Ise Moritoki</a>, later called Hojo Soun, a minor official with ties to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-clan">Imagawa</a>, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izu-province">Izu</a> in the 1490s and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> castle, traditionally in 1495. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujitsuna">Ujitsuna</a> adopted the prestigious surname Hojo, recalling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> regents, though the families were unrelated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Hojo carried out land surveys, registered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> by their military obligations and simplified taxes, building one of the most systematic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku</a> administrations. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujiyasu">Hojo Ujiyasu</a> won a celebrated victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-kawagoe-castle">Kawagoe</a> in 1546 and expanded across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a>, resisting attacks by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Uesugi Kenshin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> grew into a large walled castle town.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujimasa">Hojo Ujimasa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-ujinao">Ujinao</a> refused to submit to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, who besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a> with an immense army in 1590. After its surrender Ujimasa was ordered to kill himself and Ujinao was exiled; their lands went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, who made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-tokyo">Edo</a> his base.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1495 CE – 1590 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Korea and Japan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.45%;width:1.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1495 CE – 1590 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Odawara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hojo Soun, Hojo Ujiyasu, Hojo Ujimasa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Later Hojo clan, Go-Hojo, Hojo of Odawara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1542&amp;focus=later-hojo-clan-domain" aria-label="Later Hojo clan domain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8202 903 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Later Hojo clan domain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8522 1159L8519 1128M8522 1159L8440 1178M8522 1159L8522 1159"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8519 1128h0M8440 1178h0M8522 1159h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8522 1159h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8522 1159h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Odawara. <a href="/atlas?year=1542&amp;focus=later-hojo-clan-domain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
